{
  "0": "Interaction mechanism: replace dot-product compatibility with hᵀdiag(1+0.1·tanh(a))e, where a is jointly trained and initialized to zero. This bounded diagonal bilinear scorer may emphasize predictive interest dimensions while limiting overfitting. Preserve the GRU, input features, embeddings, history readout, loss and optimizer.",
  "1": "Feature construction: multiply each existing input item embedding by 1/sqrt(1+c), where c counts earlier occurrences of that item in the available causal history. This deterministic repeat-frequency feature may reduce domination by repeated purchases and expose broader interests. Preserve embedding parameters and dimensions, GRU topology, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer; compute the same feature at inference without accessing future interactions.",
  "2": "Network architecture: change only the GRU reset gate to r=0.1+0.9·sigmoid(a_r), retaining the existing update gate and candidate equations. A small reset floor may preserve useful recurrent context when reset activations saturate near zero, without adding layers or increasing sequence cost. Preserve hidden width, embeddings, features, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer.",
  "3": "Sequence modeling: halve the existing maximum causal context length, rounding up, and retain the most recent interactions in chronological order. Shorter histories may remove stale preferences and reduce recurrent computation while preserving recent purchase intent. Apply identical truncation during training and prediction; preserve supplied splits, feature definitions, embeddings, GRU topology, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer. Keep all four category routes and one trained checkpoint per category."
